WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.601
-Guys, today is Friday,
and that's usually

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.868
when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.167
You know, I check my in-box,
return some e-mails,

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.734
and, of course,
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:09.200
I was running
a bit behind today.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.567
I was just wondering,

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.200
can I write out some weekly
thank-you notes right now?

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.367
Is that okay with you guys?

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:16.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:19.367
James, can I get some thank-you-
note-writing music, please?

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:22.300
[ Piano plays ]

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.868
What's he doing?

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:25.167
Is he chewing something?

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:26.367
-I think he's had
his second Maple Pepsi.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:28.701
-He's, like, hiding something
in his mouth.

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:30.033
-Is it a bird?
Is a bird in there?

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:31.267
-I don't know what it is.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:33.901
He had a jalapeño slice
of pizza, maybe, earlier.

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:35.234
-Pizza pie?
-Yeah, pizza pie.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.701
-Spicy pizza pie.
-Yeah.

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:38.167
[ Laughs ]

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:39.467
[ Piano plays ]

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.734
Thank you, Oscar pools,

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:43.801
for giving me a chance to win
back some of the money I lost

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.067
on my March Madness bracket.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:46.133
Yeah.

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:48.400
[ Applause ]

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.501
I lost so much ApeCoin,
you have no idea.

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:51.667
-How much ApeCoin did you lose?

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:54.400
-Oh, my God, I lost like...

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.534
35 Jimmy Bucks'
worth of ApeCoin.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:59.567
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:00.934
[ Piano plays ]

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:04.067
Thank you, picture from
this week's NATO summit,

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:05.367
for letting me know
what it'd look like

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.701
if Brooks Brothers sponsored
a new "We Are the World."

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:10.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:13.234
♪ There comes a time ♪

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:15.501
♪ When we heed a certain call ♪

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:16.934
[ Notes play ]

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:21.667
[ Piano plays ]

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:24.767
Thank you, Harry Styles'
new album cover

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.000
for "Harry's House,"

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.501
for looking like
that moment you realized

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.100
you built the IKEA backwards.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.267
You go --
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:37.200
[ Piano plays ]

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.801
Thank you, March,

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.501
for feeling like someone
put the weather on shuffle.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.534
[ Laughter and applause ]
It's like I --

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:45.801
Come on!

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.300
"It's beautiful today!"

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.834
-It's 20!
-Wearing a turtleneck.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.400
[ Piano plays ]

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.701
Thank you, senioritis,
for being, by far,

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:58.167
the best "itis" you can have
after spring break.

00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:00.200
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:06.167
[ Piano plays ]

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:08.133
Thank you, March Madness,

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.100
for going from
"I hope I win my office pool"

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:13.067
to "I'll just be happy
if Chad from HR loses."

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:14.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:20.501
Why?
-Wow, you hate Chad.

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:21.801
[ Piano plays ]

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:23.701
-Thank you, birdhouses,

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.834
or as the Airbnb listing
calls it,

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:27.000
"kind of a hole in the wall."

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:35.300
[ Piano plays ]

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.534
Thank you, Questlove,
for being nominated

00:02:37.534 --> 00:02:40.334
for an Academy Award
for Best Documentary...

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:42.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:47.467
...and for being
the only nominee

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.567
who could end their speech

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:50.234
by playing their own
wrap-it-up music.

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:52.133
There you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:53.968
Good luck to you, buddy.
There you have it.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:55.467
Those are our thank-you notes.

